enum NexusModDetailV2Fixtures {
    static let zebrusCore = #"{"data":{"mods":{"nodes":[{"modId":49246,"description":"[b][color=#ff7700][size=3]I use AI for this mod (image creation, research, planning, translation, and source code optimization). If you don't like that, you're [/size][/color][color=#ff0000][size=3]free [/size][/color][color=#ff7700][size=3]to choose [/size][/color][color=#ff0000][size=3]not [/size][/color][color=#ff7700][size=3]to use this mod![/size][/color] [/b]\n<br />\n<br />[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]\n<br />[color=#D4D4D8]Zebrus Core adds a shared, in-game search menu that other Zebrus mods can plug into. It handles the text search box, a dynamic filter row, the results list, the detail view, keyboard/mouse/controller/mobile input, and a \"My Location\" button that jumps the location filter to wherever you're currently standing.\n<br />\n<br />Filters shown in the menu adapt automatically to whatever mod is being searched. For example, Zebrus Where is my Fish shows season, weather, catch category and catch status filters, while Zebrus Where is my NPC shows gender and marriageable filters instead. Filters with no relevant data for the current search are hidden automatically rather than shown empty.\n<br />\n<br />Zebrus Core also exposes a small mod-to-mod API so other mods (including ones I haven't built yet) can register their own searchable data without needing to reimplement the menu, filtering, or input handling from scratch.[/color]\n<br />\n<br />[size=4][b]Language[/b][/size]\n<br />[size=3]English and German[/size]\n<br />\n<br />[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]\n<br />[color=#D4D4D8]- SMAPI 4.0.0 or later\n<br />- Stardew Valley 1.6 or later[/color]\n<br />\n<br />[size=4][b]Optional[/b][/size]\n<br />- Generic Mod Config Menu (for the in-game settings menu)\n<br />\n<br />[b][size=4]Compatibility[/size][/b]\n<br />- Multiplayer/split-screen safe. Should work alongside virtually any other mod, since it doesn't change any vanilla game data or behavior by itself."}]},"modFiles":[{"version":"1.0.0","date":1784217894,"changelogText":["Initial release. Adds the shared search menu framework used by Zebrus Where is my Fish and Zebrus Where is my NPC. Supports a dynamic, auto-hiding filter system, keyboard, controller and mobile input, and a My Location button. Provides a mod-to-mod API for other Zebrus mods to register searchable data."]},{"version":"1.0.1","date":1784449708,"changelogText":["Filters with no relevant data now hide automatically instead of showing empty. My Location can now fill in your actual location even if nothing currently matches it. Adds support for showing detail values as icons instead of plain text."]},{"version":"1.1.0","date":1784452423,"changelogText":["Adds a placeholder icon for entries with no valid picture, instead of showing nothing or a broken image."]},{"version":"1.2.0","date":1784571452,"changelogText":["Icons are now drawn preserving their aspect ratio instead of stretched to fill their box.","Adds a placeholder icon for entries with no valid picture.","Adds support for entries that need to render their icon on demand (used by player portraits in Zebrus Where is my NPC).","The \"featured today\" list highlight (e.g. birthday) can now show a custom reason and rank above or below other reasons instead of a single fixed label."]},{"version":"1.3.0","date":1784653214,"changelogText":["Adds a \"season only\" option to the season filter (e.g. \"Fall only\" instead of just \"Fall\"), for fish that are exclusively available in one season."]},{"version":"1.4.0","date":1784828771,"changelogText":["Location names in filters now use the location's own DisplayName when a mod provides one, instead of always deriving a name from its internal ID."]},{"version":"1.5.0","date":1784910633,"changelogText":["Adds a second, larger icon that a result can show in its detail view and results list (used by Zebrus Where is my Item to preview a container).","Adds an always-visible list suffix (used to show an item's total quantity directly in the results list). Results list icons now preserve their aspect ratio."]},{"version":"1.6.0","date":1784973111,"changelogText":["Adds a \"Clear Filters\" button next to \"My Location\" that resets every filter back to none.","Adds support for mods to configure default filter values (used by Zebrus Where is my Fish and Zebrus Where is my NPC) and to apply the same location/season/weather defaults as \"My Location\" automatically on open. Fixes the Category, Caught status, and Marriageable filters disappearing when narrowing by mod happened to exclude every entry with that flag set (e.g. picking a mod whose fish hadn't been caught yet used to hide the Caught filter entirely, even with other caught fish elsewhere)."]},{"version":"1.7.0","date":1785089206,"changelogText":["On Android, the search menu now automatically shows fewer result rows if needed so the whole menu fits on screen without being cut off, based on the actual screen height. No change on PC/Mac/Linux.","Widens the \"Clear Filters\" button slightly so longer translations (e.g. German) fit properly."]},{"version":"1.7.1","date":1785175480,"changelogText":["Fixes Chinese/Japanese/Korean filter labels (\"Mod\", \"Location\", etc.) showing as asterisks instead of the translated text - they now use the same font as the rest of the menu for those languages.","On Android, filter dropdown option lists can now be scrolled by dragging the scrollbar (previously only mouse wheel worked, which doesn't exist on touch devices)."]},{"version":"1.8.0","date":1785267938,"changelogText":["Adds a new public API method (GetLocationDisplayName) that dependent Zebrus mods now use, replacing what used to be a separately-maintained location translation list in each mod","fixes many previously untranslated locations at once (Farmhouse, Greenhouse, Caldera, Beach Night Market, Ginger Island, and dozens more), based on a comprehensive community-maintained reference list.","Adds an optional label shown next to a result's small preview image in the list (used by Zebrus Where is my Item to show a container's custom name)."]},{"version":"1.8.1","date":1785428766,"changelogText":["Fixes a compatibility issue between Core and the other Zebrus search mods (Fish/NPC/Item) that could prevent the search menu from connecting to Core at all."]},{"version":"1.8.2","date":1785574753,"changelogText":["Fixes the search text field not reliably getting keyboard focus when opening the menu via hotkey (only worked if you moved the mouse over it first).","Fixes the \"Cindersap Forest\" location showing with an incorrect German translation (\"Aschensaft-Wald\" instead of \"Zundersaftwald\")."]},{"version":"1.9.0","date":1785665766,"changelogText":["Fixes the \"Farm\" location showing untranslated in every non-English language.","Adds a new capability for \"Where is my X\" mods to prioritize a specific location in their own sorting (used by Zebrus Where is my Item's new location-priority feature).","Fixes the \"Farm\" location showing untranslated in every non-English language.","Adds a new capability for \"Where is my X\" mods to prioritize a specific location in their own sorting (used by Zebrus Where is my Item's new location-priority feature)."]},{"version":"1.9.0","date":1785668658,"changelogText":["Fixes the \"Farm\" location showing untranslated in every non-English language.","Adds a new capability for \"Where is my X\" mods to prioritize a specific location in their own sorting (used by Zebrus Where is my Item's new location-priority feature).","Fixes the \"Farm\" location showing untranslated in every non-English language.","Adds a new capability for \"Where is my X\" mods to prioritize a specific location in their own sorting (used by Zebrus Where is my Item's new location-priority feature)."]},{"version":"1.9.1","date":1785860711,"changelogText":["Filter dropdowns are now sorted by their displayed name in your language, so the location list (and others) read in proper alphabetical order.","The season filter is now ordered by calendar (Spring, Summer, Fall, Winter), each season directly followed by its \"only\" variant."]},{"version":"1.10.0","date":1786119276,"changelogText":["Legendary fish are now highlighted in the results list and detail view, with a distinct style for the quest-only \"extended family\" legendary variants.","Filter dropdowns now support type-ahead: with a dropdown open, start typing to jump to the first matching entry, without typing into the search box."]}]}}"#

    static let sveExcerpt = #"{"data":{"mods":{"nodes":[{"modId":3753,"description":"[center][url=https://twitter.com/FlashShifter][/url][/center]\n<br />[center]﻿[/center]\n<br />[center][url=https://twitter.com/FlashShifter][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1303/images/7608/7608-1610385311-241093688.png[/img]﻿﻿﻿﻿[/url]\n<br />[color=#b6b6b6][i]The world of Stardew Valley"}]},"modFiles":[{"version":"1.14.14","date":1655053348,"changelogText":["***Content***","Added an installation checker that informs players in the SMAPI console if SVE is correctly installed or not. Huge thanks to Shekurika and Moe from the Ridgeside Village development team!","Players can now invite Scarlett to the movie theater.","Scarlett now attends community day.","Apples now plays with Peaches on sunny Fridays and attends all festivals if rooming with the player.",".","***Gameplay Changes***","Recolored the shalal shrub, ancient fern and rafflesia.","Simplified the internal code that prevents the mermaid's bracelet, galdoran gem, super starfruit, and aurora vineyard property deed from being gifted.","Increased the rarity of four leaf clovers in the western cindersap forest.","Increased forage spawns in the highlands ruins area during summer and fall.","Increased sea shell spawns at Fable Reef.",".","***Bugs***","Fixed an issue where Treyvon displayed an invisible frame during Scarlett's 6 heart event.","Fixed an issue where Sophia's reading animation didn't work in some instances during community day.","Fixed an issue where Pierre clipped into Caroline during community day.","Fixed an issue where players could gift the galdoran gem.","Fixed an issue where some players couldn't unlock the warp point to Aurora Vineyard if they were rooming with Apples.","Fixed an issue where Apples' became a roommate option upon seeing their 10 heart part 2 instead of part 3.","Fixed an issue where the CJB Cheats secret woods warp teleported players into a cliff.","Fixed an issue where Apples' icon didn't show up on the map if rooming with the player and NPC Map Locations was installed.","Fixed an issue where Lance had incorrect movie film reaction IDs."]},{"version":"1.14.14","date":1655053456,"changelogText":["***Content***","Added an installation checker that informs players in the SMAPI console if SVE is correctly installed or not. Huge thanks to Shekurika and Moe from the Ridgeside Village development team!","Players can now invite Scarlett to the movie theater.","Scarlett now attends community day.","Apples now plays with Peaches on sunny Fridays and attends all festivals if rooming with the player.",".","***Gameplay Changes***","Recolored the shalal shrub, ancient fern and rafflesia.","Simplified the internal code that prevents the mermaid's bracelet, galdoran gem, super starfruit, and aurora vineyard property deed from being gifted.","Increased the rarity of four leaf clovers in the western cindersap forest.","Increased forage spawns in the highlands ruins area during summer and fall.","Increased sea shell spawns at Fable Reef.",".","***Bugs***","Fixed an issue where Treyvon displayed an invisible frame during Scarlett's 6 heart event.","Fixed an issue where Sophia's reading animation didn't work in some instances during community day.","Fixed an issue where Pierre clipped into Caroline during community day.","Fixed an issue where players could gift the galdoran gem.","Fixed an issue where some players couldn't unlock the warp point to Aurora Vineyard if they were rooming with Apples.","Fixed an issue where Apples' became a roommate option upon seeing their 10 heart part 2 instead of part 3.","Fixed an issue where the CJB Cheats secret woods warp teleported players into a cliff.","Fixed an issue where Apples' icon didn't show up on the map if rooming with the player and NPC Map Locations was installed.","Fixed an issue where Lance had incorrect movie film reaction IDs."]},{"version":"1.14.14","date":1655053477,"changelogText":["***Content***","Added 